List this repository's worktrees with their state, the URL of the first service
that loads (and how many more there are) and their directory. Outside a
repository, or with --all, it lists every registered worktree on the machine,
with the repository first, and needs no treerig.toml. A URL is shown only while
its service runs and the router's container is up; nothing is fetched over HTTP.
On a terminal, stderr also says how many directories are gone and, inside a
repository, where the overview page is. --refresh, with --all (or outside a
repository), rebuilds the overview page under the router's lock; otherwise list
takes no lock and writes nothing. It exits 0, and 1 when Docker didn't answer:
the table is still printed, with unknown states.

Usage:
  treerig list [flags]

Aliases:
  list, ls

Flags:
      --all             every repository on this machine
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd, if
                        any)
  -h, --help            help for list
      --json            machine-readable output
      --refresh         rebuild the overview page (needs --all inside a
                        repository)

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
